    <chapter id="ch_e3d74c02" title="Opening Scene">

      <p>&lt;p&gt;In the dim back room of a harbor tavern called &lt;strong&gt;The Rusty Anchor&lt;/strong&gt;, an unlikely group had gathered around a corner table.&lt;/p&gt;</p>

      <p>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mira&lt;/strong&gt; nervously plucked at the strings of her silent guitar, feeling the jealous stare of &lt;strong&gt;Clara&lt;/strong&gt; behind her. The bespectacled student methodically cleaned her glasses while checking something in a battered notebook.&lt;/p&gt;</p>

      <p>&lt;p&gt;A little farther away, &lt;strong&gt;Bran&lt;/strong&gt; sat lazily sipping cheap rum. His tattooed fingers tapped out an irregular rhythm against the wooden table.&lt;/p&gt;</p>

      <p>&lt;p&gt;From the kitchen came the clatter of pots and pans. &lt;strong&gt;Gareth&lt;/strong&gt; was arguing with a supplier again, his booming voice carrying through the entire tavern.&lt;/p&gt;</p>

      <p>&lt;p&gt;At the bar, &lt;strong&gt;Victor&lt;/strong&gt; looked bored, tossing a shiny coin into the air and catching it without even looking.&lt;/p&gt;</p>

      <p>&lt;p&gt;A few minutes later, &lt;strong&gt;Selene&lt;/strong&gt; swept into the room with the confidence of someone who expected everyone to stop and watch her. Her bright makeup contrasted sharply with her strict business suit.&lt;/p&gt;</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter id="ch_9af7a318" title="Dialogue">

      <scene title="Tensions in the Rusty Anchor" mood="Tense">
        <location>The Rusty Anchor Tavern</location>
      </scene>

      <p>
        <line char="mira">— If we don't start the show in five minutes, the audience is going to tear this place apart,</line>
        <line char="narrator">— squeaked the little singer, pushing a loose strand of blonde hair back into her ponytail.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="clara">— Calm down,</line>
        <line char="narrator">— replied the girl with glasses dryly without looking up from her notes.</line>
        <line char="clara">— According to my calculations, the crowd won't reach its peak for another thirty minutes.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="narrator">The old boatswain gave a low chuckle through his mustache and finished his rum.</line>
        <line char="bran">— Your calculations forgot that three cargo ships were unloaded at the harbor today. There's nowhere left to stand.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="gareth">— And who's going to pay for all the broken dishes?</line>
        <line char="narrator">— shouted the mustached cook from behind the kitchen curtain, waving a wooden ladle threateningly.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="narrator">A lazy voice came from the corner of the bar.</line>
        <line char="victor">— Relax, chef. My people are controlling the entrance. We won't let anyone extra inside,</line>
        <line char="narrator">— said the grim bouncer, catching the falling coin in his palm.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="narrator">At that moment the doors swung open, and the demanding diva entered the room with a theatrical sigh.</line>
        <line char="selene">— What a dump. You can practically smell the cheap beer and stale ale.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="mira">— Oh, look who's finally here,</line>
        <line char="narrator">— sneered the singer, deliberately turning her back toward the wall.</line>
        <line char="mira">— We've only been waiting for you for an hour, Your Highness.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="selene">— Traffic, darling,</line>
        <line char="narrator">— said the model, waving dismissively while inspecting her flawless manicure.</line>
        <line char="selene">— Besides, my time is worth more than this little concert of yours.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="narrator">The top student finally closed her notebook and gave the newcomer a stern look.</line>
        <line char="clara">— We're supposed to work as a team. Your ego is destroying the entire schedule.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="selene">— We've heard your lectures before,</line>
        <line char="narrator">— snorted the brunette, walking toward the mirror beside the stage.</line>
        <line char="selene">— Where's our sponsor?</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="bran">— Our distinguished investor,</line>
        <line char="narrator">— answered the sea dog,</line>
        <line char="bran">— is currently calculating the losses from the last storm. So we'll have to manage on our own.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="gareth">— Wonderful,</line>
        <line char="narrator">— muttered the chef, returning to the stove.</line>
        <line char="gareth">— That means I'll probably miss another bonus for the banquet.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="bran">— Stop whining,</line>
        <line char="narrator">— growled the tattooed bruiser, getting up from his chair.</line>
        <line char="bran">— Hey, bartender, pour me another one before these strings snap.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="narrator">The big guy behind the counter silently filled a glass and pushed it toward the musician.</line>
        <line char="victor">— That's the last one on the house. After that, you pay full price.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="selene">— Hey, the college student,</line>
        <line char="narrator">— called the tall fashionista from the stage,</line>
        <line char="selene">— hand me that microphone. And be careful. Don't dirty the cable.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="narrator">The fair-haired girl flushed with indignation.</line>
        <line char="mira">— What, did your hands fall off? Get it yourself. I'm not your servant!</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="victor">— Ladies, break it up,</line>
        <line char="narrator">— the man keeping order said lazily.</line>
        <line char="victor">— If you start a fight, I'll throw both of you out without severance pay.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="clara">— Fine,</line>
        <line char="narrator">— sighed the bespectacled student.</line>
        <line char="clara">— Guitarist ready. Vocals ready. We start on the first signal.</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="narrator">From the kitchen came the final chord of the kitchen master's culinary symphony.</line>
        <line char="gareth">— Good riddance! Just stay away from my serving counter!</line>
      </p>

      <p>
        <line char="bran">— Well then, here we go,</line>
        <line char="narrator">— grinned the old sailor, taking one final sip and winking at the fair-haired girl.</line>
      </p>

      <scene_end>Tensions in the Rusty Anchor</scene_end>
    </chapter>
  </body>
</ovml>
```
